    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "McGovern Estates is delighted to present 20 Woodlands Court to the market - a rare penthouse residence occupying a superb position within one of Greystones' most sought-after developments.\r\n\r\nSet amongst mature, private grounds and just a short stroll from the seafront, this spacious penthouse combines an enviable coastal setting with wonderful potential to create a truly exceptional home. Elevated above its surroundings, the property enjoys far-reaching views towards the Irish Sea from the living room, principal bedroom and private balcony - a feature that gives the apartment a distinctive sense of space and connection to its setting.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation has a wealth of character and natural light, with vaulted ceilings, dormer windows and a series of Velux skylights adding volume and brightness throughout the principal living areas. At the heart of the apartment, the generous living and dining room is centred around a striking marble fireplace with an electric fire, while sliding doors open directly onto the private balcony - an ideal vantage point from which to enjoy the sea views and the changing light throughout the day. \r\n\r\nThe generously proportioned kitchen features granite worktops and excellent storage, while its configuration presents an exciting opportunity for transformation.The existing partition between the kitchen and living/dining area could be removed, subject to the necessary consents, creating an impressive open-plan kitchen, living and entertaining space tailored to the vision of the next owner. The accommodation extends to three well-proportioned double bedrooms. The principal bedroom enjoys sea views and benefits from a separate walk-in dressing room and en-suite facilities. While the penthouse would benefit from modernisation, its exceptional setting, generous proportions, architectural character and outstanding views provide an exciting canvas for a future owner to create a sophisticated coastal residence of considerable distinction.\r\n\r\nWoodlands Court enjoys a superb location within easy walking distance of Greystones town centre and harbour marina. The surrounding area offers an excellent choice of restaurants, cafés, shops and leisure amenities, with the beach, playing pitches and coastal walks all close at hand. Greystones DART station and local bus services provide convenient access to Dublin city and beyond, while the N11 is also readily accessible.\r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION\r\nEntrance Hallway\r\nSolid wood flooring, intercom, bespoke radiator cover, skylight.\r\n\r\nLiving Room\r\nSolid maple wood flooring, open electric fire with polished marble mantle and hearth, wall uplights, electric heater, recessed lighting, feature walk-in bay window with magnificent views of the sea and mature common areas, sliding doors to balcony. Ample eaves storage.\r\n\r\nKitchen\r\nTiled flooring, fully fitted kitchen, floor and wall-based storage cupboards, ample polished granite countertops, integrated appliances, inset stainless steel sink, recessed lighting, 2 Velux windows.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\nLaminated wood flooring, Feature dormer bay window with magnificent sea views and surrounding mature common areas, walk-in wardrobe with ample storage and hanging rails. Electric wall heater, recessed lighting, \r\n\r\nEn-suite\r\nTiled flooring, WC, wash hand basin with under-storage, Siemens electric wall heater, fully tiled shower with mains power shower, extractor fan, skylight window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\r\nSolid maple wood flooring, floor to ceiling built-in wardrobe, electric wall heater, recessed lighting, walk-in dormer bay window overlooking west-facing communal garden. Ample eaves storage.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\r\nLaminated wood flooring, electric wall heater, recessed lighting, walk-in bay dormer window.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom\r\nTiled flooring, part tiled walls, Victorian cistern WC, pedestal wash hand basin, part tiled bath, fully tiled shower with mains power shower, Dimplex wall heater, recessed lighting, extractor fan.\r\n\r\nBalcony\r\nPrivate balcony with slate tiles. Wonderful views of the Irish Sea.\r\n\r\nOutside Rear\r\nWest-facing communal garden. \r\n\r\nOutside Front\r\nAmple off street parking near front door. A columned entrance porch with white double doors featuring decorative glass panels, flanked by Granite pillars and a small brass nameplate. A paved path leads up through neat hedging, framed by mature silver birch trees - giving the entrance a smart, established feel.\r\n\r\nShared Rear Garden\r\nCommunal secure bicycle storage shed to rear."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Penthouse apartment within Woodlands Court, set in mature, private grounds\r\nServiced by a lift\r\nMagnificent sea views from the living room, main bedroom and private balcony\r\nPrivate tiled balcony/terrace off living area\r\nPotential to remove partition wall to the living/dining area, creating one large open-plan kitchen/living/dining space\r\nVaulted ceilings throughout with dormer windows\r\nVelux skylights over the kitchen and living room\r\nAmple storage area in eaves \r\nFeature marble fireplace with electric fireplace\r\nSolid wood flooring in the hallway, Bedroom 2 and living/dining area\r\nNew laminate wood floors in Bedroom 1 and Bedroom 3\r\nMain bedroom with full-height mirrors in bay window with sea views\r\nSeparate walk-in wardrobe/dressing room off the main bedroom\r\nEn-suite off the main bedroom\r\nKitchen with granite worktops and ample storage\r\nSouth and west facing well-maintained communal gardens with mature trees, lawn and patio seating area\r\nPrivate parking\r\nSecure bicycle storage shed (communal)\r\nShort walk to Greystones beach, harbour, playing pitches and town centre\r\nClose to Greystones DART station with Park & Ride facilities\r\nEasy access to the N11 for Dublin and beyond"
